-- title:
--   Base change of the q-expansion function field is a function field
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of finite index containing the translation matrix `ModularGroup.T`. Write $F =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set `intFormRatiosC`, namely by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$ where, for some weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, $f$ and $g$ are modular forms of weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, $p_f, p_g$ are power series with integer coefficients satisfying the predicate `IsIntegralQExp` with respect to $f$ and to $g$ respectively, and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g \neq 0$. Let `laurentBaseChange L F` be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image of $F$ under the coefficientwise ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. The assertion is that there exists an element $x$ of `laurentBaseChange L F` which is transcendental over $L$ and such that `laurentBaseChange L F` is finite-dimensional as a vector space over the intermediate field $L(x)$ generated over $L$ by $x$.
--
--   This is the statement that the base change to $L$ of the $q$-expansion presentation of the function field of the modular curve attached to $\Gamma$ is an algebraic function field of one variable over $L$, obtained from the corresponding statement over $\mathbb{Q}$. It is the hypothesis under which the general theory of one-variable function fields (places, divisors, genus, Jacobian) is applied to modular curves in the subsequent development, and it is invoked throughout the treatment of $X_1(M)$ and its Jacobian.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JOneES_exists_transcendental_finiteDimensional_laurentBaseChange.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X1

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.JOneES.exists_transcendental_finiteDimensional_laurentBaseChange
    (L : Type*) [Field L] [Algebra ℚ L]
    (Γ : Subgroup (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℤ)) [Γ.FiniteIndex]
    (hT : ModularGroup.T ∈ Γ) :
    ∃ x : ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ),
      Transcendental L x ∧
      FiniteDimensional
        (IntermediateField.adjoin L
          ({x} : Set (ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ))))
        (ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ)) := by sorry
